Chapter: RocRecWrapperMatch
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_recursive_data_tests.zig,
 "inspect: recursive tag payload match issue 8754":

     Tree := [Node(Str, List(Tree)), Text(Str), Wrapper(Tree)]
     inner : Tree = Text("hello")
     wrapped : Tree = Wrapper(inner)
     main = match wrapped {
         Wrapper(inner_tree) => match inner_tree { Text(_) => 1, Node(_, _) => 2, Wrapper(_) => 3 }
         _ => 0 }

 Roc answers 1. `Text` is a Codex type name, so the constructor is `Leaf`.
 The inner match is on a name bound by the outer pattern, which is the
 shape the Roc issue was about.

Section: Types

  Tree =
   | Node (Text) (List Tree)
   | Leaf (Text)
   | Wrapper (Tree)

Section: Functions

  classify : Tree -> Integer
  classify (wrapped) =
   when wrapped
    is Wrapper (inner-tree) -> when inner-tree
      is Leaf (ignored) -> 1
      is Node (ignored) (kids) -> 2
      is Wrapper (ignored) -> 3
    is otherwise -> 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let inner = Leaf "hello"
   in let wrapped = Wrapper inner
   in print-line-uni (show (classify wrapped))
  end
